  "design_review": {
    "scope": "C60 accepted production algorithm with test-only attribution. No C62-C65 queue/scoped/claim code included.",
    "source_revision": "0243b5f1ef6beb37da2e157758647b85d78444f9",
    "native_tree": "c686c0b8e485f45629d9806db99c48d59cf3aedc",
    "production_file_diff": "dependencies.rs changes only cfg(test) memo point parameters/arguments, candidate start/finish hooks, fixture arguments and formatting. Existing ordinary memo/column ownership, ordering and data operations are unchanged. worker_phase_probe and nested joins module are beneath the existing cfg(test) module declaration. Normal release compilation and observer-symbol scan both succeeded.",
    "normal_binary": "Hash differs from C60; no byte identity to preceding baseline is assumed or claimed. Actual merged hash must later be compared to this selected normal library.",
    "measurement_contract": [
      "A candidate begins only after observing an unfinished OnceLock and is recorded only if this call did not run its initializer. Initially ready calls and owned initializer execution are excluded. A racing publication or preemption may be included; memo intervals also include result cloning.",
      "Candidate stores only scalar tag/token/time/key, with no Arc clone, collector lock or event allocation for initializer candidates. Materialized noninitializer events use the physical worker collector. No dependency-cell, planner, world or GPU owner is retained.",
      "Thread-local context frames form a RAII stack; tags distinguish tasks even in the same root. Context and candidate are non-Send/non-Sync via PhantomData<Rc<()>>. Nested A->B->A restores the outer collector even if LOCAL.bind last saw B.",
      "Context mismatches fail the diagnostic. Non-LIFO task termination is counted and invalidates completed-window attribution. Active contexts at root completion also invalidate it.",
      "Task Drop emits a failed span; Trace Drop records an abandoned failed root with available/missing phases. Root Drop empties task/join buffers on every path, including summary failure, while TLS retains at most collector shells.",
      "Before intersection, all events are validated against evaluation and corresponding physical-thread task unions. Reversed/outside/unjoined evidence is not silently clipped into valid data. Missing evaluation remains null.",
      "Intervals are unioned by physical worker; category unions and different workers can overlap in wall time. Task and tail intersections have explicit units. Task time outside these joins is not classified as CPU; terrain/GPU waits and probe overhead can be outside coverage.",
      "Only scalar phase/event counts, summaries and bounded longest samples persist; raw buffers are released after each joined root. Observer overhead remains inside complete generation."
    ],
    "tests": {
      "existing": 167,
      "new": 5,
      "total_passed": 172,
      "failed": 0,
      "ignored": 48,
      "new_cases": [
        "Ready and owned exclusion with an actual other-thread OnceLock error owner; exact original error preserved.",
        "Nested root and initializer panic restore outer attribution; abandoned root/missing phases and failed tasks retained.",
        "Mismatched context rejected and non-LIFO tasks flagged invalid.",
        "Overlapping physical-worker API joins unioned; category overlaps and exact p95-tail intersections verified.",
        "Missing phases, reversed/outside/no-task evidence and unjoined contexts cannot produce valid attribution."
      ],
      "gpu_parity": 1
    },
    "limitations": [
